.TH SETRESGID 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setresgid \- sets real, effective and saved group ids; (gid_t)-1 leaves an id unchanged
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int setresgid(gid_t real, gid_t effective, gid_t saved);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets real, effective and saved group IDs; (gid_t)-1 leaves an ID unchanged. This is a direct per-thread syscall.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setresgid (2)
